  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "26.1.3.40: Built against DX.Data.Xpo.Identity 26.1.3.40 (security fix: redeemed recovery codes stayed valid; lockout is persisted; see its release notes). LockoutEnd is mapped to LockoutEndDateUtc. The stores use a mapper of their own: AddXpoMapsterIdentityStores no longer writes the identity rules into TypeAdapterConfig.GlobalSettings (which also made parallel registrations throw). Behaviour change: code that maps identity types through GlobalSettings itself must call RegisterXPIdentityMapsterConfiguration(); ApplyXPIdentityMapsterConfiguration(config) adds the rules to a config of your own.\n\t\t\t26.1.3.39: Rebuilt against DX.Data.Xpo.Identity 26.1.3.39 (the Microsoft.Extensions.Identity packages per target framework (8.0 for net8.0, 9.0 for net9.0, 10.0 for net10.0): 10.0 on net8.0 brought Microsoft.AspNetCore.Cryptography.Internal 10 into .NET 8 apps and broke Data Protection (tokens, antiforgery) on Linux.)\n\t\t\t26.1.3.37: Rebuilt against DX.Data.Xpo.Identity 26.1.3.37 / DX.Data.Xpo.Mapster 26.1.3.34 to pick up the System.Security.Cryptography.Xml 8.0.4 fix (NU1903) transitively.\n\t\t\t26.1.3.36: Added a README.md with technical documentation, now embedded in the package via PackageReadmeFile.\n\t\t\t26.1.3.35: Rebuilt against DX.Data.Xpo.Identity 26.1.3.35 / DX.Data.Xpo.Mapster 26.1.3.32 to pick up DevExpress v26.1.3 transitively.",
